Z||000003||fiero56||10-24-1999||07:20 PM||||Why did you guys do this?  I hate the way my Fiero looks if the lights are on.  The only reason I believe somone would want do this is so they don't freeze shut during the winter.  Hmm, funny, I was just asking myself today, how am I going to keep those lids from freezing shut when the snow comes. How'd you guys do the wiring, and where'd you put the switch?||||reg||5
Z||000004||kornholio||10-24-1999||08:21 PM||||The snow is coming to Ontario soon and I don't want my headlights to get stuck down.  <BR>Check out the instructions for the wiring at the Michigan Fiero Club (http://www.tir.com/~jaski/headlight.htm)<BR>I took off the cover under the steering column and cut a retangular opening at the lip for the switch.  You can't even see the switch at all.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||10-25-1999||02:34 AM||||I was thinking of doing this as well.  I have a rear window defroster button, but no rear window defroster.    Granted it is not a toggle switch, but it could be used to lower the lights by holding it down untill the lights are fully down then releasing it(by using it in line with the white wire which is connected to the headlight switch).  My defroster switch has no wires going to it or connected to it, but if someone knows why this is a bad idea let me know.||||reg||1
